\citation{kirkpatrick2017overcoming}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {One process serves and learns.} Top: the fused loop. Every token is served by one forward pass; a two-timescale surprise gate decides per window whether that same pass also becomes a learning step. When it fires, a \emph  {cascade kick} routes output errors backward through the routing caches the forward already produced---gather/scatter/add only, no second forward, no stored activation graph---and steps the optimizer in place; the next token is served by the updated weights. Bottom: the substrate, a tropical (max-plus) MorphSSM language model in which every mixing operation is a maximum of sums or a gather, so the winning paths cached during serving are exactly the table needed to assign credit without multiplication.}}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:loop}{{2}{4}{\textbf {One process serves and learns.} Top: the fused loop. Every token is served by one forward pass; a two-timescale surprise gate decides per window whether that same pass also becomes a learning step. When it fires, a \emph {cascade kick} routes output errors backward through the routing caches the forward already produced---gather/scatter/add only, no second forward, no stored activation graph---and steps the optimizer in place; the next token is served by the updated weights. Bottom: the substrate, a tropical (max-plus) MorphSSM language model in which every mixing operation is a maximum of sums or a gather, so the winning paths cached during serving are exactly the table needed to assign credit without multiplication}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Predictive coding, made exact and deep by the substrate.} \textbf  {a}, The cascade update equals backpropagation's gradient: over all 282 parameter-tensor checks the cosine similarity is $1.000$ and the relative error is $\sim \!10^{-7}$ (floating-point summation order); synchronous relaxation is bitwise identical and asynchronous, partial-participation sweeps recover the exact gradient (cosine $\in \{0,1\}$: routed or not-yet-arrived). \textbf  {b}, On a 128-layer residual network the multiplication-free cascade is the only method that still trains; floating-point backpropagation collapses toward chance and naive iterative predictive coding sits at chance for every depth (mean$\pm $s.d., three seeds). \textbf  {c}, On our own tropical sequence model the cascade tracks backpropagation's validation cross-entropy at every depth (mean$\pm $s.d., three seeds). Data: \texttt  {g0\_gradcheck}, \texttt  {g1\_equivalence}, \texttt  {scale\_mnist\_128layer}, \texttt  {g3\_g4\_*}.}}{5}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:depth}{{3}{5}{\textbf {Predictive coding, made exact and deep by the substrate.} \textbf {a}, The cascade update equals backpropagation's gradient: over all 282 parameter-tensor checks the cosine similarity is $1.000$ and the relative error is $\sim \!10^{-7}$ (floating-point summation order); synchronous relaxation is bitwise identical and asynchronous, partial-participation sweeps recover the exact gradient (cosine $\in \{0,1\}$: routed or not-yet-arrived). \textbf {b}, On a 128-layer residual network the multiplication-free cascade is the only method that still trains; floating-point backpropagation collapses toward chance and naive iterative predictive coding sits at chance for every depth (mean$\pm $s.d., three seeds). \textbf {c}, On our own tropical sequence model the cascade tracks backpropagation's validation cross-entropy at every depth (mean$\pm $s.d., three seeds). Data: \texttt {g0\_gradcheck}, \texttt {g1\_equivalence}, \texttt {scale\_mnist\_128layer}, \texttt {g3\_g4\_*}}{figure.caption.4}{}}
\citation{hu2022lora}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The loop pays, self-calibrates, and is not dominated.} \textbf  {a}, Headroom captured on three short single-regime streams (gated learner, mean over three seeds). \textbf  {b}, The gate law: a self-normalized $z$-gate fires at a fixed quantile regardless of regime (stationary and shifted indistinguishable), while the two-timescale absolute-margin gate self-quiets on stationary data and storms at shifts. \textbf  {c}, Quality versus extra update compute on identical streams: our two operating points hold the low-compute frontier; no incumbent cell lies below-and-left of ours, and matching our quality costs a tuned LoRA-periodic incumbent $3.3\times $ our update budget and a $2.7\times $ activation-memory class (single seed on the incumbent sweep; our side three-seed). Data: \texttt  {v2\_live}, \texttt  {v3\_lora}.}}{7}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:validation}{{4}{7}{\textbf {The loop pays, self-calibrates, and is not dominated.} \textbf {a}, Headroom captured on three short single-regime streams (gated learner, mean over three seeds). \textbf {b}, The gate law: a self-normalized $z$-gate fires at a fixed quantile regardless of regime (stationary and shifted indistinguishable), while the two-timescale absolute-margin gate self-quiets on stationary data and storms at shifts. \textbf {c}, Quality versus extra update compute on identical streams: our two operating points hold the low-compute frontier; no incumbent cell lies below-and-left of ours, and matching our quality costs a tuned LoRA-periodic incumbent $3.3\times $ our update budget and a $2.7\times $ activation-memory class (single seed on the incumbent sweep; our side three-seed). Data: \texttt {v2\_live}, \texttt {v3\_lora}}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {A lifelong stream of experience: one process, ten million tokens, five rotated domain cycles.} \textbf  {a}, Prequential cross-entropy of the live learner (blue) versus its frozen twin (grey); shaded bands mark domains, dotted lines mark cycles. The learner storms down at each first encounter, then serves revisits almost for free, while the frozen twin re-pays the full cost forever. \textbf  {b}, Gate fire rate; learning kicks collapse from 1{,}275 to 45 per cycle. \textbf  {c}, Held-out probe cross-entropy per domain at every era boundary---after the first cycle the stability--plasticity trade is stable and improves with revisits (bounded, non-increasing interference). \textbf  {d}, Weight norm reaches equilibrium ($+2.3\%$ over the life; slope decelerates twelvefold). Data: \texttt  {v4\_tele\_main}, \texttt  {v4\_probes\_main}.}}{8}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:lifelong}{{5}{8}{\textbf {A lifelong stream of experience: one process, ten million tokens, five rotated domain cycles.} \textbf {a}, Prequential cross-entropy of the live learner (blue) versus its frozen twin (grey); shaded bands mark domains, dotted lines mark cycles. The learner storms down at each first encounter, then serves revisits almost for free, while the frozen twin re-pays the full cost forever. \textbf {b}, Gate fire rate; learning kicks collapse from 1{,}275 to 45 per cycle. \textbf {c}, Held-out probe cross-entropy per domain at every era boundary---after the first cycle the stability--plasticity trade is stable and improves with revisits (bounded, non-increasing interference). \textbf {d}, Weight norm reaches equilibrium ($+2.3\%$ over the life; slope decelerates twelvefold). Data: \texttt {v4\_tele\_main}, \texttt {v4\_probes\_main}}{figure.caption.6}{}}
